#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to read and interpret the open-source notice, the security report, and the open-source risk report that BomLens produces."
msgstr "如何閱讀與解讀 BomLens 產生的開放原始碼授權聲明、安全報告與開放原始碼風險分析報告。"

#. type: Title #
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "What the reports mean"
msgstr "如何解讀報告"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:8
msgid ""
"This page explains how to read and interpret BomLens reports after a scan. "
"For how to produce them, see [Generating reports](../guides/reports.md)."
msgstr "這一頁說明掃描結束後如何閱讀與解讀 BomLens 的報告。其產生方式請看[產生報告](../guides/reports.md)。"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "What the notice handles"
msgstr "授權聲明的處理內容"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:12
msgid ""
"The open-source notice (NOTICE) groups components by license. Beyond that "
"grouping, it also handles the following."
msgstr ""
"開放原始碼授權聲明 (NOTICE) 會依授權條款把元件分組。除了分組之外，它還一併處"
"理下列事項。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:17
msgid ""
"It normalizes license names to SPDX identifiers. For example, \"Apache "
"License, version 2.0\" is normalized to `Apache-2.0`. Entries that were "
"duplicated because the same license was written differently are merged into "
"one."
msgstr ""
"把授權條款名稱正規化為 SPDX 識別碼。例如「Apache License, version 2.0」會正規"
"化為 `Apache-2.0`。同一份授權條款因為寫法不同而重複的項目，會合併成一項。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:17
msgid ""
"When the scan tool could not name a license and left it as `CUSTOM` with the "
"license file text attached (common for Go modules whose LICENSE file "
"rewrites the copyright lines), the text itself is checked against the "
"wording of major licenses (`MIT`, `BSD-2-Clause`, `BSD-3-Clause`, "
"`Apache-2.0`, `ISC`) and the SPDX identifier is recovered. A text that stays "
"ambiguous is kept as `CUSTOM` rather than guessed."
msgstr "掃描工具無法判定授權條款名稱，僅留下 `CUSTOM` 並附上授權條款檔全文時（常見於 LICENSE 檔改寫著作權標示行的 Go 模組），會將全文與主要授權條款（`MIT`、`BSD-2-Clause`、`BSD-3-Clause`、`Apache-2.0`、`ISC`）的條文用語進行比對，以還原 SPDX 識別碼。若比對後仍無法明確判定授權條款，則會保留為 `CUSTOM`，而不會逕行推測。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:17
msgid "If the SBOM has a copyright value, it is shown per component."
msgstr "SBOM 裡有著作權 (copyright) 值時，會逐一元件顯示。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:17
msgid ""
"The full SPDX standard texts of 21 major open-source licenses (`Apache-2.0`, "
"`MIT`, `BSD-3-Clause`, the `GPL`/`LGPL` families, and so on) are bundled at "
"the end of the notice. This satisfies the obligation of licenses that "
"require the full text, without separate collection. The bundled originals "
"are in `docker/lib/licenses/*.txt`."
msgstr "21 種主要開放原始碼授權條款（`Apache-2.0`、`MIT`、`BSD-3-Clause`、`GPL`／`LGPL` 家族等）的 SPDX 標準全文，也會附在授權聲明的最後。如此即可履行須隨附授權條款全文的義務，無須另外蒐集。這些內建的授權條款全文位於 `docker/lib/licenses/*.txt`。"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "Priority signals (CVSS, EPSS, CISA KEV)"
msgstr "優先順序訊號（CVSS、EPSS、CISA KEV）"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:21
msgid ""
"Severity alone makes it hard to decide what to fix first. To help with that, "
"the security report shows three more signals beyond severity. The Markdown "
"and HTML table columns are `Severity | KEV | CVSS | EPSS | CVE | Package | "
"Installed | Fixed`."
msgstr ""
"只看嚴重程度很難決定該先修哪一個。為此，安全報告在嚴重程度之外還提供三個訊"
"號。Markdown 與 HTML 表格的欄位組成是 `Severity | KEV | CVSS | EPSS | CVE | "
"Package | Installed | Fixed`。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:25
msgid ""
"**CVSS** — the technical severity score of the vulnerability (0–10). The V3 "
"score is used first, falling back to V2 if absent."
msgstr ""
"**CVSS**——弱點的技術性嚴重程度分數 (0–10)。優先採用 V3 分數，沒有時才後備採"
"用 V2。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:25
msgid ""
"**EPSS** — the probability of real-world exploitation within the next 30 "
"days (0–1). Queried from FIRST.org; a higher score means a greater chance of "
"being used in an attack."
msgstr ""
"**EPSS**——未來 30 天內在真實環境遭到利用的機率 (0–1)。查詢自 FIRST.org；分數"
"越高，被用於攻擊的機會越大。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:25
msgid ""
"**CISA KEV** — whether it is on the \"known exploited vulnerabilities\" list "
"maintained by the US CISA. If it is, the HTML report marks it with a ⚠️ badge."
msgstr ""
"**CISA KEV**——是否列在美國 CISA 維護的「已知遭利用弱點」清單中。列在其中時，"
"HTML 報告會以 ⚠️ 標記標示。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:27
msgid ""
"The table puts KEV-listed items at the top, then sorts by severity, and "
"finally by EPSS descending. Working top-down naturally addresses the highest-"
"risk items first. This is specific to the static report file; the [web UI's "
"vulnerabilities table](../reference/ui.md#result-sections) opens sorted by "
"severity then CVSS instead, and lets you re-sort by any column, including "
"EPSS."
msgstr ""
"表格會把列在 KEV 中的項目排在最前面，接著依嚴重程度排序，最後再依 EPSS 遞減排"
"序。由上往下處理，自然就會先處理風險最高的項目。這套排序只適用於靜態的報告檔"
"案；[網頁介面的弱點表格](../reference/ui.md#result-sections)開啟時是先依嚴重"
"程度、再依 CVSS 排序，而且可以依任一欄位重新排序，包括 EPSS。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:29
msgid ""
"EPSS and KEV require external API lookups. On an air-gapped network, set "
"`SECURITY_ENRICH=false` to omit the two columns and still generate the rest "
"of the report."
msgstr ""
"EPSS 與 KEV 需要向外部 API 查詢。在封閉網路中，可以設定 "
"`SECURITY_ENRICH=false`，略過這兩欄，報告其餘部分照樣產生。"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "Outbound-license conflicts"
msgstr "對外授權條款衝突 {#outbound-license-conflicts}"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "The license classification above labels each component's copyleft strength on its own. Whether that strength is actually a problem depends on the license *you* distribute under, which a source scan cannot infer — so you declare it with `--license <spdx-id>` (or the web UI's Outbound license field), and each dependency is then judged against it.\n"
msgstr "上面的授權分類只就各元件本身標示它的 Copyleft 強度。那個強度是否真的構成問題，取決於*你*對外散布時採用的授權條款，而原始碼掃描無法推斷這個值——所以要用 `--license <spdx-id>`（或網頁介面的「對外授權條款」欄位）宣告它，之後每個相依項目都會以它為基準判定。\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:37
msgid ""
"`Cannot be met` — the dependency's terms cannot be satisfied while shipping "
"under your declared license."
msgstr "`無法滿足`——以所宣告的授權條款散布時，無法同時滿足該相依項目的條件。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:37
msgid ""
"`Depends on how you ship` — permitted, but the obligations turn on how you "
"link or distribute. A person has to look."
msgstr ""
"`視散布方式而定`——允許，但義務取決於你如何連結或散布。需要有人親自確認。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:37
msgid "`Cannot judge` — the license was not recognised, or you declared none."
msgstr "`無法判定`——授權條款未被辨識，或是你沒有宣告任何對外授權條款。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:39
msgid ""
"A license carrying an exception clause (the classpath exception being the "
"common one) never lands in the first bucket: that clause exists precisely to "
"permit the combination."
msgstr ""
"帶有例外條款的授權條款（最常見的是 classpath 例外）絕不會落到第一類：那條條款"
"存在的目的，正是為了允許這樣的組合。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:41
msgid ""
"Declare nothing and the check does not run — the report simply omits the "
"section rather than printing a clean bill nobody checked. It is a "
"documentation aid, not a legal determination: see the [CLI reference](../"
"reference/cli.md) for the flag and [Web UI](../reference/ui.md) for where "
"the verdicts appear."
msgstr ""
"什麼都不宣告，這項檢查就不會執行——報告會直接省略該區段，而不是印出一份沒人檢"
"查過的無問題結論。它是協助準備文件的資料，不是法律判定：旗標請看[CLI 參考]"
"(../reference/cli.md)，判定顯示的位置請看[網頁介面](../reference/ui.md)。"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "Known-malicious packages"
msgstr "已知惡意套件"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:45
msgid ""
"A vulnerability says an honest package has a flaw. A malicious package is a "
"different thing: it was published to attack whoever installs it — a "
"typosquat of a name you meant to type, a release pushed from a hijacked "
"maintainer account, a payload that runs during installation. BomLens flags "
"these separately from the vulnerability table, because the response is "
"different. You remove the package, and you rotate any credential the build "
"could reach; there is no version to upgrade to."
msgstr ""
"弱點指的是一個正常的套件有缺陷。惡意套件性質不同：它是為了攻擊安裝它的人而發"
"佈的——針對你想輸入的名稱所做的錯字仿冒 (typosquat)、從被挾持的維護者帳號推上"
"去的發行版本，或是在安裝過程中執行的惡意程式碼。BomLens 把這類項目與弱點表格"
"分開標示，因為應對方式不一樣。你必須移除該套件，並輪替建置過程可能接觸到的所"
"有認證資訊；沒有可以升級過去的版本。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:50
msgid ""
"Matching is by PURL, never by name. These packages are deliberately named to "
"resemble real ones, so a name match is exactly the wrong tool."
msgstr ""
"比對一律以 PURL 進行，絕不用名稱。這類套件刻意取得與真品相似的名稱，用名稱比"
"對正好是最不該用的方式。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:50
msgid ""
"The data is a bundled snapshot of the malicious-package advisories OSV "
"publishes (the ones carrying a `MAL-` id), so the check runs offline like "
"the EOL flag. Set `ENRICH_MALICIOUS=false` to skip it."
msgstr ""
"資料是 OSV 所發佈的惡意套件公告（帶有 `MAL-` 識別碼的那些）的內建快照，因此這"
"項檢查和已終止支援標記一樣可以離線執行。設定 `ENRICH_MALICIOUS=false` 可以略"
"過它。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:50
msgid ""
"Most advisories name no versions, which means every published version of "
"that package is malicious. When an advisory does name versions, only those "
"are flagged."
msgstr ""
"大多數公告沒有指明版本，意思是該套件所有已發佈的版本都是惡意的。公告確實指明"
"版本時，只會標記那些版本。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:50
msgid ""
"Each flagged component carries the advisory id and the snapshot date "
"(`bomlens:malicious:id`, `bomlens:malicious:source`). The date matters: this "
"is a fast-moving area, so a clean result means \"not in this snapshot\", not "
"\"safe today\"."
msgstr ""
"每個被標記的元件都會帶著公告識別碼與快照日期（`bomlens:malicious:id`、"
"`bomlens:malicious:source`）。日期很重要：這個領域變化很快，所以什麼都沒查到"
"只代表「不在這份快照裡」，不代表「今天是安全的」。"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:51
#, no-wrap
msgid "Component end-of-life (EOL)"
msgstr "元件已終止支援 (EOL) {#component-end-of-life-eol}"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:54
msgid ""
"BomLens also flags whether each component's release cycle has reached its "
"upstream end-of-life. This is a supply-chain risk separate from CVEs: a "
"runtime or framework past its support date gets no more upstream security "
"fixes, so a Critical or High reported later has no patch to apply."
msgstr "BomLens 也會標示各元件的發行週期是否已達上游的支援終止期限（End-of-Life，EOL）。這是與 CVE 各自獨立的供應鏈風險：超過支援期限的執行環境或框架不會再獲得上游提供的安全性修正，因此之後即使通報 Critical（嚴重）或 High（高）等級的弱點，也沒有修補程式可供套用。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:59
msgid ""
"The dates come from a snapshot of endoflife.date bundled into the scanner "
"image, so the check runs offline with no network call and works air-gapped. "
"The source and snapshot date are recorded on each flagged component "
"(`bomlens:eol:source`)."
msgstr ""
"日期來自內建於掃描器映像檔的 endoflife.date 快照，因此這項檢查不需任何網路呼"
"叫就能離線執行，封閉網路也能用。來源與快照日期會記錄在每個被標記的元件上"
" (`bomlens:eol:source`)。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:59
msgid ""
"Coverage follows endoflife.date, which tracks runtimes, major frameworks, "
"operating systems and databases (spring-boot, express, django, nodejs, "
"python, php, nginx, openssl, ubuntu, debian, and so on). Most smaller "
"libraries are not tracked, and a component with no mapping is left unknown "
"rather than guessed."
msgstr ""
"涵蓋範圍以 endoflife.date 為準，它追蹤的是執行環境、主要框架、作業系統與資料"
"庫（spring-boot、express、django、nodejs、python、php、nginx、openssl、"
"ubuntu、debian 等）。多數規模較小的函式庫不在追蹤範圍內；沒有對應資料的元件會"
"保留為未知，不會用猜測值填補。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:59
msgid ""
"In the web UI, the Overview shows an \"End of life\" count tile, with the "
"components that are also vulnerable highlighted in the risk colour — an EOL "
"component gets no upstream patch for its CVEs, so that is the set to act on. "
"The Components table adds an \"End of life\" badge, with the EOL date where "
"known, and an \"End of life\" filter."
msgstr ""
"在網頁介面中，「總覽」會出現一個「已終止支援」計數方塊，其中同時有弱點的元件"
"會以風險色標示——已終止支援的元件不會再有上游修補來處理它的 CVE，所以那正是該"
"動手的一批。「元件」表格則會多出「已終止支援」標記（知道終止日期時一併顯示）"
"與「已終止支援」篩選條件。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:59
msgid ""
"It is on by default and adds no delay because it is offline. To turn it off, "
"set `ENRICH_EOL=false`. AI/ML model scans skip it, since they have no "
"runtime or framework components."
msgstr ""
"它預設開啟，而且因為是離線執行所以不會拖慢速度。想關掉就設定 "
"`ENRICH_EOL=false`。AI／ML 模型掃描會略過這個步驟，因為它們沒有執行環境或框架"
"元件。"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:60
#, no-wrap
msgid "Version currency"
msgstr "版本新舊 {#version-currency}"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:63
msgid ""
"Sitting on a supported release cycle is not the same as running its latest "
"version, so BomLens also flags whether a component has fallen behind. This "
"works in two layers."
msgstr ""
"待在受支援的發行週期裡，並不等於用的是該週期的最新版本，所以 BomLens 也會標示"
"元件是否已經落後。這項判定分成兩層。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:67
msgid ""
"The offline layer is on by default, alongside the EOL check. The same "
"endoflife.date snapshot records the latest patch of each release cycle, so "
"BomLens can tell offline whether the installed version trails the newest "
"patch within its own cycle. That is a safe, in-cycle upgrade found with no "
"network call, exactly like the EOL check. A component that is behind carries "
"`bomlens:currency:outdated=true`, with the target patch in "
"`bomlens:currency:latestPatch`. It runs inside the EOL step, so "
"`ENRICH_EOL=false` turns it off as well, and AI/ML model scans skip it."
msgstr ""
"離線層與已終止支援檢查一起預設開啟。同一份 endoflife.date 快照記錄了各發行週"
"期的最新修補版本，所以 BomLens 能離線判斷已安裝的版本是否落後於它自己週期內的"
"最新修補版本。這是一次不需網路呼叫就能找出的、安全的週期內升級，和已終止支援"
"檢查完全一樣。落後的元件會帶上 `bomlens:currency:outdated=true`，目標修補版本"
"則放在 `bomlens:currency:latestPatch`。它是在已終止支援的步驟裡執行的，因此 "
"`ENRICH_EOL=false` 會一併把它關掉，AI／ML 模型掃描也會略過。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:67
msgid ""
"The deps.dev layer is opt-in. Set `STALENESS_ENRICH=true` to look each "
"component up on deps.dev, Google's public package metadata, and record the "
"absolute newest version (`bomlens:staleness:latest`), how many releases the "
"installed one is behind (`bomlens:staleness:releasesBehind`), and when the "
"newest version shipped (`bomlens:staleness:lastReleased`). This makes one "
"network call per component, so it trades the scan's offline determinism for "
"freshness. It does not suit an air-gapped run, which is why it is off by "
"default. It is best-effort and time-bounded, so a failed lookup never aborts "
"the scan. The supported ecosystems are npm, PyPI, Maven, Go, Cargo, NuGet "
"and RubyGems. Whether a project is still actively maintained is not part of "
"this release; it is planned for a later release."
msgstr ""
"deps.dev 層是 opt-in。設定 `STALENESS_ENRICH=true` 之後，會把每個元件拿到 "
"deps.dev（Google 的公開套件後設資料）查詢，記錄絕對最新的版本"
" (`bomlens:staleness:latest`)、已安裝的版本落後幾個發行版本"
" (`bomlens:staleness:releasesBehind`)，以及最新版本是什麼時候發行的"
" (`bomlens:staleness:lastReleased`)。它每個元件都會發出一次網路呼叫，因此是"
"拿掃描的離線決定性去換資料的新鮮度。它不適合封閉網路的執行環境，所以預設關"
"閉。它是盡力而為且有時間上限的，因此查詢失敗絕不會中斷掃描。支援的生態系有 "
"npm、PyPI、Maven、Go、Cargo、NuGet 與 RubyGems。專案是否仍在積極維護不在這個"
"版本的範圍內，會留到後續版本。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:67
msgid ""
"In the web UI, the Overview adds a count tile for components behind their "
"latest version, and the Components table marks a component that is not on "
"its latest version and adds an \"Outdated\" filter. With the deps.dev layer "
"on, each such component also shows how many releases it is behind and its "
"last-release date."
msgstr ""
"在網頁介面中，「總覽」會多出一個方塊，統計落後於最新版本的元件數；「元件」表"
"格則會把不是最新版本的元件標示為「非最新」，並多出一個「非最新」篩選條件。開"
"啟 deps.dev 層之後，這類元件還會顯示落後幾個版本以及最後一次發行的日期。"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:68
#, no-wrap
msgid "Interpreting results & follow-up"
msgstr "結果解讀與後續處理"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:76
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Severity | Meaning | Recommended action |\n"
"|----------|---------|--------------------|\n"
"| **Critical** | immediately exploitable, severe | upgrade to the `Fixed` version as the top priority |\n"
"| **High** | high risk | plan a patch in the short term |\n"
"| **Medium / Low** | limited impact | handle during regular maintenance |\n"
"| **Unknown** | severity not assessed | check the CVE directly and classify |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Severity | 意義 | 建議做法 |\n"
"|----------|---------|--------------------|\n"
"| **Critical（嚴重）** | 可立即被利用，影響嚴重 | 最優先處理——升級到 `Fixed` 欄位所列的版本 |\n"
"| **High（高）** | 風險高 | 在短期內排定修補計畫 |\n"
"| **Medium（中）／ Low（低）** | 影響有限 | 於例行維護時處理 |\n"
"| **Unknown（未知）** | 尚未評估嚴重程度 | 直接查看該 CVE 後自行分類 |\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:79
msgid ""
"If the report's `Fixed` column has a version, raising the dependency to that "
"version or higher resolves it. This is the fastest first response."
msgstr ""
"報告的 `Fixed`（修正版本）欄位有版本時，把相依項目提升到該版本或更高就能解"
"決。這是最快的第一線應對。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:79
msgid "CI gate example. Fail the build if there is even one Critical:"
msgstr "CI 關卡範例。只要有一件 Critical（嚴重）就讓建置失敗："

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:79
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  crit=$(jq '[.Results[]?.Vulnerabilities[]? | select(.Severity==\"CRITICAL\")] | length' *_security.json)\n"
"  [ \"$crit\" -gt 0 ] && { echo \"${crit} Critical vulnerabilities\"; exit 1; }\n"
msgstr ""
"  crit=$(jq '[.Results[]?.Vulnerabilities[]? | select(.Severity==\"CRITICAL\")] | length' *_security.json)\n"
"  [ \"$crit\" -gt 0 ] && { echo \"${crit} 個 Critical 弱點\"; exit 1; }\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:84
msgid ""
"Triage — judging false positives (no real impact) and approving exceptions — "
"and history management are beyond the scope of BomLens. Upload the SBOM to a "
"vulnerability management system (Dependency-Track, TRUSCA, etc.) to handle "
"it."
msgstr ""
"分級處理 (triage)——判斷誤判（實際上沒有影響）與核准例外——以及歷程管理，都超"
"出 BomLens 的範圍。請把 SBOM 上傳到弱點管理系統（Dependency-Track、TRUSCA "
"等）來處理。"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:85
#, no-wrap
msgid "The open-source risk report"
msgstr "開放原始碼風險分析報告"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:88
msgid ""
"The open-source risk report aggregates vulnerabilities by severity with "
"recommended response deadlines (Critical 7 days, High 30 days). It includes "
"a license summary, and for a supplier SBOM it adds the format conformance "
"result."
msgstr ""
"開放原始碼風險分析報告會依嚴重程度彙整弱點，並附上建議的應對期限（Critical"
"（嚴重）7 天、High（高）30 天）。它內含授權條款摘要；分析供應者 SBOM 時，還會"
"加上格式符合性結果。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:90
msgid ""
"The license summary also classifies components by copyleft strength, with "
"the same rules the web UI uses. Each component in the SBOM carries a "
"`bomlens:licenseClass` property holding one of `network-copyleft`, `strong-"
"copyleft`, `weak-copyleft`, `permissive` or `uncategorized`, and the report "
"shows a per-class count plus the components that drive the copyleft "
"exposure. A license the tool does not recognize is never assumed permissive; "
"it stays `uncategorized` for a human to review."
msgstr ""
"授權條款摘要也會依 Copyleft 強度把元件分類，規則與網頁介面所用的相同。SBOM 中"
"每個元件都帶有 `bomlens:licenseClass` 屬性，值為 `network-copyleft`、`strong-"
"copyleft`、`weak-copyleft`、`permissive` 或 `uncategorized` 之一；報告會顯示"
"各分類的數量，以及造成 Copyleft 曝險的那些元件。工具無法辨識的授權條款絕不會"
"逕自視為 permissive，而是保留為 `uncategorized`，交由人工檢視。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:95
msgid "[Generating reports](../guides/reports.md)"
msgstr "[產生報告](../guides/reports.md)"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:95
msgid "[Artifacts reference](../reference/artifacts.md)"
msgstr "[產出物參考](../reference/artifacts.md)"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/reports-explained.md:95
msgid "[How BomLens works](architecture.md)"
msgstr "[BomLens 的運作原理](architecture.md)"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "What an SBOM (Software Bill of Materials) is, why open-source notices and vulnerability response depend on one, and what CycloneDX, PURL, and ML-BOM mean — a five-minute primer before your first scan."
msgstr "SBOM（Software Bill of Materials，軟體物料清單）是什麼、為什麼開源授權聲明與弱點應變都得靠它，以及 CycloneDX、PURL、ML-BOM 各代表什麼——第一次掃描前的五分鐘入門。"

#. type: Title #
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "What is an SBOM"
msgstr "什麼是 SBOM"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:8
msgid ""
"An SBOM (Software Bill of Materials) is a list of the components inside a "
"piece of software: every open-source library and package it ships with, each "
"with its name, version, and license. It plays the same role for software "
"that a list of ingredients plays for packaged food — you can see what is "
"inside without taking the product apart."
msgstr ""
"SBOM（Software Bill of Materials，軟體物料清單）是一份軟體內部元件的清單：軟"
"體隨附的每一個開放原始碼函式庫與套件，連同各自的名稱、版本與授權條款。它對軟"
"體的作用，就像成分表對包裝食品一樣——不必把產品拆開，就能看見裡面有什麼。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:10
msgid ""
"Most software today is assembled largely from open source. A typical web "
"application directly declares a few dozen packages, and those pull in "
"hundreds more. Nobody can keep that inventory in their head, so the SBOM is "
"generated from the project by a tool — that is what BomLens does."
msgstr ""
"今天大多數軟體都是以開放原始碼組裝出來的。一個典型的網頁應用程式直接宣告的套"
"件有數十個，而這些套件又會再帶進數百個。沒有人能把這份清冊記在腦子裡，因此 "
"SBOM 是由工具從專案產生的——BomLens 做的就是這件事。"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why you need one"
msgstr "為什麼需要 SBOM"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:14
msgid ""
"Two everyday jobs depend on knowing exactly what is inside your software."
msgstr "有兩件日常工作，取決於你是否確切知道軟體裡有什麼。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Meeting license obligations.** Most open-source licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, and others) require you to ship a copyright notice and the license text along with your product. To write that open-source notice you first need the component list — the SBOM. BomLens generates the notice from the SBOM in the same run.\n"
msgstr "**履行授權義務。**大多數開放原始碼授權條款（MIT、Apache-2.0、BSD 等）要求你在產品中隨附著作權標示與授權條款全文。要寫出這份開放原始碼授權聲明，首先得有元件清單，也就是 SBOM。BomLens 會在同一次執行中，直接由 SBOM 產生授權聲明。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Responding to vulnerabilities.** When a vulnerability is announced in a library, the first question is \"do we ship it, and in which version?\". With an SBOM per product, that answer is a lookup instead of an investigation. This is also why customers and regulators increasingly ask suppliers to hand over an SBOM with each delivery.\n"
msgstr "**弱點應變。**當某個函式庫被公告有弱點時，第一個問題是「我們的產品有用到它嗎，用的是哪個版本？」。只要每個產品都有 SBOM，這個答案就是一次查詢，而不是一場調查。這也是客戶與監理機關越來越常要求供應者在每次交付時一併提供 SBOM 的原因。\n"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:19
#, no-wrap
msgid "Terms you will meet in the results"
msgstr "在結果中會遇到的名詞"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "**CycloneDX** is the standard file format BomLens writes its SBOMs in — a JSON document defined by the [OWASP CycloneDX](https://cyclonedx.org/) project (version 1.6). Because the format is standard, the file you generate can be read by other tools: vulnerability trackers, policy checkers, or a customer's own tooling.\n"
msgstr "**CycloneDX** 是 BomLens 寫出 SBOM 所採用的標準檔案格式——由 [OWASP CycloneDX](https://cyclonedx.org/) 專案定義的 JSON 文件（1.6 版）。正因為格式是標準的，你產生的檔案可以被其他工具讀取：弱點追蹤系統、政策檢查工具，或是客戶自己的工具。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:24
#, no-wrap
msgid "**PURL** (Package URL) is the identifier each component carries inside the SBOM, such as `pkg:npm/express@4.18.2`. It names the ecosystem (npm, Maven, PyPI, and so on), the package, and the exact version in one string, so every tool that reads the SBOM agrees on which component is meant.\n"
msgstr "**PURL** (Package URL) 是 SBOM 內部每個元件所帶的識別碼，例如 `pkg:npm/express@4.18.2`。它以一個字串同時記下生態系（npm、Maven、PyPI 等）、套件與確切版本，讓每個讀取這份 SBOM 的工具都對「指的是哪個元件」有一致的理解。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/what-is-sbom.md:26
#, no-wrap
msgid "**ML-BOM** is the same idea applied to an AI model: a CycloneDX document listing what a model is made of — its datasets, base model, and license. BomLens generates one from a HuggingFace model id; see the [AI model guide](../guides/ai-model.md).\n"
msgstr "**ML-BOM** 是把同樣的概念套用到 AI 模型上：一份 CycloneDX 文件，列出一個模型由什麼構成——它的資料集、基礎模型與授權條款。BomLens 可以從 HuggingFace 模型 ID 產生一份；請參考 [AI 模型指南](../guides/ai-model.md)。\n"

