#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generate an AI SBOM (CycloneDX ML-BOM) for a HuggingFace model with BomLens and check it against the G7 minimum elements for AI — the 50-element checklist whose clusters overlap with the EU AI Act's Annex IV technical documentation. From the model id, no source code or model download needed."
msgstr "以 BomLens 為 HuggingFace 模型產生 AI SBOM (CycloneDX ML-BOM)，並依 AI 的 G7 最低要素檢查——這份 50 項要素的檢查清單，其叢集與 EU AI Act 的 Annex IV 技術文件有相當程度的重疊。只要給模型 id，不需要原始碼，也不需要下載模型。"

#. type: Title #
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "AI model SBOM guide"
msgstr "AI 模型 SBOM 指南"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:8
msgid ""
"How to generate a CycloneDX ML-BOM (machine-learning bill of materials) for "
"a HuggingFace model and read the result. You give a model id; BomLens "
"fetches the model-card metadata over the network — no source code and no "
"model-weight download."
msgstr ""
"如何為 HuggingFace 模型產生 CycloneDX ML-BOM（機器學習元件清單）並讀懂結果。"
"你給模型 id，BomLens 會透過網路取得模型卡的後設資料——不需要原始碼，也不需要下"
"載模型權重。"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:9 docs/guides/firmware.md:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "How it works"
msgstr "運作方式"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:12
msgid ""
"An AI model's \"bill of materials\" is its model card: identifier, "
"architecture, task, license, supplier, datasets, and the integrity of its "
"files. BomLens uses the [OWASP AIBOM Generator](https://github.com/GenAI-"
"Security-Project/aibom-generator) to read a HuggingFace model card and build "
"a **CycloneDX 1.7 ML-BOM** centered on the model and the datasets it "
"references. It then adds a **G7 minimum-element conformance** check "
"(advisory). Because a model has no package dependencies, there is no "
"security (CVE) report."
msgstr ""
"AI 模型的「元件清單」就是它的模型卡：識別碼、架構、任務、授權條款、供應者、資"
"料集，以及檔案的完整性。BomLens 以 [OWASP AIBOM Generator](https://"
"github.com/GenAI-Security-Project/aibom-generator) 讀取 HuggingFace 模型卡，"
"建立一份以模型與它所參考的資料集為中心的 **CycloneDX 1.7 ML-BOM**，接著加上一"
"輪 **G7 最低要素符合性**檢查（建議性質）。由於模型沒有套件相依性，因此不會產"
"生安全 (CVE) 報告。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:14
msgid ""
"The model is the subject of the document: it sits in `metadata.component`, "
"which is where CycloneDX names what an SBOM is about, and the datasets it "
"references sit under `components[]` as its dependencies. A tool reading the "
"ML-BOM should look for the model there rather than in the component list."
msgstr ""
"模型是這份文件所描述的對象：它位在 `metadata.component`，也就是 CycloneDX 用"
"來記載「這份 SBOM 是關於什麼」的位置，而它所參考的資料集則以相依項目的形式放"
"在 `components[]` 底下。讀取 ML-BOM 的工具應該到那個位置找模型，而不是到元件"
"清單裡找。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:16
msgid ""
"A model card names its training datasets and stops there. BomLens looks each "
"one up on HuggingFace and records what it finds — the declared license, the "
"upstream datasets it derives from, and a content digest — as its own entry "
"in the SBOM, linked to the model as a dependency. A dataset that cannot be "
"read (withdrawn, renamed, or private to someone else) is kept in the SBOM as "
"a name marked unreadable; no license is invented for it. This is also what "
"decides the training-data disclosure axis: `open-data` needs at least one "
"dataset that actually opened, and a card naming datasets nobody can retrieve "
"reads `declared-unverified` instead."
msgstr ""
"模型卡只列出訓練資料集的名稱就結束了。BomLens 會逐一到 HuggingFace 查詢，把查"
"到的內容——宣告的授權條款、它所衍生自的上游資料集，以及內容雜湊值——以獨立項目"
"的形式寫進 SBOM，並以相依關係連到模型。讀不到的資料集（已撤下、改名，或屬於他"
"人的私有儲存庫）會保留名稱並標示為無法讀取，不會為它憑空補上授權條款。訓練資"
"料揭露這一軸也由此決定：要成為 `open-data`，必須至少有一個資料集真的打開了；"
"模型卡列了名稱但誰都取不到，讀出來會是 `declared-unverified`。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:18
msgid ""
"The full tool flow is in [Pipeline by input type](../concepts/pipeline-by-"
"input.md#ai-model)."
msgstr ""
"完整的工具流程請看[各輸入類型的流程](../concepts/pipeline-by-input.md#ai-"
"model)。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:22
msgid "You need two things."
msgstr "你需要兩樣東西。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:25
msgid ""
"**A Docker engine, installed and running.** If you have none, start with the "
"requirements in [Getting started](../start/first-scan.md)."
msgstr ""
"**已安裝並正在執行的 Docker 引擎。**如果還沒有，請先看[快速開始](../start/"
"first-scan.md)的需求說明。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:25
msgid ""
"**A way to run BomLens.** The desktop app needs no commands; for the command "
"line, [Getting started](../start/first-scan.md) covers cloning the "
"repository. AI model scans need a separate image that bundles the OWASP "
"AIBOM Generator. It is opt-in and reaches the network (HuggingFace), so it "
"ships separately from the base image."
msgstr ""
"**一種執行 BomLens 的方式。**桌面版應用程式不需要下任何指令；要用指令列的話，"
"[快速開始](../start/first-scan.md)說明了如何 clone 儲存庫。AI 模型掃描需要另"
"一個內含 OWASP AIBOM Generator 的映像檔。它是 opt-in 的，而且會連上網路"
" (HuggingFace)，因此與基礎映像檔分開發佈。"

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:26
#, no-wrap
msgid "docker pull ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens-aibom:latest\n"
msgstr "docker pull ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens-aibom:latest\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:31
msgid ""
"That image is about 3.5 GB to download, far larger than the base scanner "
"image (about 250 MB). The first pull can take tens of minutes depending on "
"your connection, so start it with time to spare. It is downloaded once."
msgstr ""
"這個映像檔的下載量約 3.5 GB，比基礎掃描器映像檔（約 250 MB）大得多。依連線速"
"度而定，第一次下載可能要花上數十分鐘，請預留時間再開始。只需要下載一次。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:33
msgid ""
"Pulling ahead of time is optional. `--model` uses this image by default and "
"fetches it when missing, and the web UI and desktop app fetch it on the "
"first AI-model scan while showing progress. To use a different tag, set "
"`SBOM_AIBOM_IMAGE`."
msgstr ""
"事先下載並非必要。`--model` 預設就使用這個映像檔，缺少時會自行取得；網頁介面"
"與桌面版應用程式也會在第一次 AI 模型掃描時取得它，並顯示進度。要改用其他標"
"籤，請設定 `SBOM_AIBOM_IMAGE`。"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:34 docs/guides/firmware.md:44
#, no-wrap
msgid "Running it"
msgstr "執行方式"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:36 docs/guides/firmware.md:48
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:28 docs/guides/upload.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "From the web UI"
msgstr "從網頁介面"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:39
msgid ""
"Use the desktop app, or the web UI you already run. Where Docker is "
"reachable the AI model tile is enabled, and the aibom image runs as a "
"separate container fetched on the first scan — which makes that first run "
"slow to start."
msgstr ""
"用桌面版應用程式，或你平常已經在跑的網頁介面都可以。只要 Docker 可連線，AI 模"
"型磁磚就會啟用，而 aibom 映像檔會在第一次掃描時取得並以獨立容器執行——這也是第"
"一次執行啟動特別慢的原因。"

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --ui\n"
msgstr "./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --ui\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:45
msgid ""
"Launching the UI from the aibom image itself handles the scan in-process, "
"with no second container. This is what you need where the Docker socket is "
"unavailable."
msgstr ""
"直接以 aibom 映像檔本身啟動網頁介面，掃描就會在同一個行程內完成，不需要第二個"
"容器。在無法使用 Docker socket 的環境就需要這種做法。"

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"SBOM_SCANNER_IMAGE=ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens-aibom:latest ./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --ui\n"
"#   Windows: set SBOM_SCANNER_IMAGE before double-clicking sbom-ui.bat\n"
msgstr ""
"SBOM_SCANNER_IMAGE=ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens-aibom:latest ./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --ui\n"
"#   Windows：雙擊 sbom-ui.bat 之前先設定 SBOM_SCANNER_IMAGE\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:52
msgid ""
"Choose **AI model** under the New scan source tiles, enter the HuggingFace "
"model id as `org/model` (for example `google-bert/bert-base-uncased` or "
"`Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B` — not a collection name or a full URL), and run."
msgstr ""
"在新掃描的來源磁磚中選擇 **AI 模型**，以 `org/model` 的格式輸入 HuggingFace "
"模型 id（例如 `google-bert/bert-base-uncased` 或 `Qwen/Qwen2.5-0.5B`——不是集"
"合名稱，也不是完整 URL），然後執行。"

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:53 docs/guides/firmware.md:65
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:41
#, no-wrap
msgid "From the CLI"
msgstr "從 CLI"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:56
msgid "Pass the model id to `--model`:"
msgstr "把模型 id 傳給 `--model`："

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:57
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --project bert-base --version 1.0.0 \\\n"
"  --model \"google-bert/bert-base-uncased\" --generate-only\n"
msgstr ""
"./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --project bert-base --version 1.0.0 \\\n"
"  --model \"google-bert/bert-base-uncased\" --generate-only\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:63
msgid ""
"`--model` is mutually exclusive with `--target`, `--analyze`, `--git`, and "
"`--merge`. It pulls the `bomlens-aibom` image automatically, produces the "
"notice and the risk report, and skips the security report (a model has no "
"package CVEs)."
msgstr ""
"`--model` 與 `--target`、`--analyze`、`--git`、`--merge` 互斥。它會自動下載 "
"`bomlens-aibom` 映像檔，產生開放原始碼授權聲明與風險報告，並略過安全報告（模"
"型沒有套件層級的 CVE）。"

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:64
#, no-wrap
msgid "Private and gated models"
msgstr "私有與受管制 (gated) 的模型 {#private-and-gated-models}"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:67
msgid ""
"A public model id resolves anonymously. A private repository, or a gated one "
"you have been granted access to, needs a HuggingFace access token with read "
"scope in `HF_TOKEN`:"
msgstr ""
"公開的模型 id 可以匿名解析。私有儲存庫，或是你已獲准存取的受管制 (gated) 儲存"
"庫，需要在 `HF_TOKEN` 中提供具備 read 權限的 HuggingFace 存取權杖："

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:68
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"HF_TOKEN=hf_... ./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --project my-llm --version 0.9.0 \\\n"
"  --model \"my-org/my-llm\" --generate-only\n"
msgstr ""
"HF_TOKEN=hf_... ./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --project my-llm --version 0.9.0 \\\n"
"  --model \"my-org/my-llm\" --generate-only\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:74
msgid ""
"`HUGGING_FACE_HUB_TOKEN` is accepted as well. The value is passed to the "
"container by name, never as a command-line argument, so it does not appear "
"in the process list, and it is not written to the SBOM or any report."
msgstr ""
"`HUGGING_FACE_HUB_TOKEN` 也可以使用。權杖的值只以名稱傳入容器，絕不會作為指令"
"列參數，因此不會出現在行程清單中，也不會寫進 SBOM 或任何報告。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:76
msgid ""
"This is what lets you review a model before you publish it: push it to a "
"private repository, generate the ML-BOM, close the gaps the conformance "
"report shows, and only then make the repository public. For a gated "
"repository, the token's account also needs its access request approved — a "
"token alone is not enough. The same token is what resolves the model's "
"training datasets, so a model whose data sits in a private repository needs "
"it too."
msgstr ""
"這正是讓你在發佈模型之前先檢視它的做法：先推到私有儲存庫，產生 ML-BOM，把符合"
"性報告指出的缺漏補起來，然後才把儲存庫轉為公開。受管制的儲存庫還需要該權杖所"
"屬帳號的存取申請已獲核准——光有權杖並不夠。解析模型的訓練資料集用的是同一個權"
"杖，所以資料放在私有儲存庫的模型也需要它。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:78
msgid ""
"The web UI reads the same variable from the environment that launched it, so "
"start it with `HF_TOKEN=hf_... ./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --ui`. There is no "
"token field in the interface: the server keeps no credentials, and a token "
"sent over HTTP would linger in its logs."
msgstr ""
"網頁介面會從啟動它的環境讀取同一個變數，因此請以 `HF_TOKEN=hf_... ./scripts/"
"scan-sbom.sh --ui` 的形式啟動。介面上沒有權杖輸入欄：伺服器不保存任何認證資"
"訊，而透過 HTTP 傳來的權杖會殘留在它的日誌裡。"

#. type: Title ###
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:79
#, no-wrap
msgid "Scanning a model file"
msgstr "掃描模型檔案"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:82
msgid ""
"Everything above starts from a model id, which assumes the model is on "
"HuggingFace. Often it is not: a supplier delivers the weights themselves, "
"the model is an internal fine-tune, or the machine has no network at all. "
"Point at the file:"
msgstr ""
"上面所有做法都從模型 id 出發，也就預設模型在 HuggingFace 上。實際上常常不是這"
"樣：供應者直接交付權重檔、模型是內部微調出來的，或是那台機器根本沒有網路。這"
"時直接指向檔案："

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:83
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --project internal-llm --version 1.0.0 \\\n"
"  --model-file ./models/internal-llm-q4.gguf --generate-only\n"
msgstr ""
"./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --project internal-llm --version 1.0.0 \\\n"
"  --model-file ./models/internal-llm-q4.gguf --generate-only\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:89
msgid ""
"In the web UI, choose **Model file** under AI model and upload it (up to 8 "
"GB; past that the CLI is the answer, because it reads the file where it lies "
"and transfers nothing)."
msgstr ""
"在網頁介面中，請在 AI 模型底下選擇**模型檔案**並上傳（最大 8 GB；超過就該用 "
"CLI，因為它會就地讀取檔案，不做任何傳輸）。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:91
msgid ""
"The file's own header is the only source, and no image is pulled — this runs "
"in the base image, offline. The format is decided by the magic bytes rather "
"than the file name, and a mismatch between the two is reported on the "
"component instead of being quietly corrected."
msgstr ""
"唯一的資料來源是檔案自身的標頭，而且不會下載任何映像檔——這是在基礎映像檔中離"
"線執行的。格式由魔術位元組 (magic bytes) 而非檔名決定，兩者不一致時會記錄在元"
"件上，而不是默默地更正過去。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:99
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Format | What the file can tell us |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| GGUF | model name, license, architecture, quantization, tensor count |\n"
"| safetensors | tensor count, dtypes, parameter count, plus whatever the optional `__metadata__` block declares (often a license) |\n"
"| PyTorch (`.pt`/`.pth`/`.ckpt`), pickle | the archive layout, and that the weights are pickle-format |\n"
"| npz, npy | the member list |\n"
"| ONNX | the format itself (deeper metadata needs a protobuf parser) |\n"
msgstr ""
"| 格式 | 檔案能告訴我們的資訊 |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| GGUF | 模型名稱、授權條款、架構、量化資訊、張量數量 |\n"
"| safetensors | 張量數量、dtype、參數數量，以及選用的 `__metadata__` 區塊所宣告的內容（通常是授權條款） |\n"
"| PyTorch（`.pt`／`.pth`／`.ckpt`）、pickle | 壓縮檔的內部結構，以及權重是 pickle 格式這件事 |\n"
"| npz、npy | 內部成員清單 |\n"
"| ONNX | 格式本身（更深入的後設資料需要 protobuf 剖析器） |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:101
msgid ""
"Every format contributes the file size and a SHA-256 over the whole file, "
"which is what ties the document to the artifact you were sent. A field the "
"file does not declare is left out: a model whose weights carry no license "
"produces an SBOM with no license, and the risk assessment then reads "
"`review` rather than treating silence as permission."
msgstr ""
"每一種格式都會附上檔案大小與整個檔案的 SHA-256，這是把文件與你收到的產出物綁"
"在一起的依據。檔案沒有宣告的欄位會直接省略：權重不帶授權條款的模型，產出的 "
"SBOM 就沒有授權條款，風險評估此時會讀成 `review`，不會把沉默當成許可。"

#. type: Title ####
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:102
#, no-wrap
msgid "Does loading it run code?"
msgstr "載入它會執行程式碼嗎？"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:105
msgid ""
"Pickle is not a data format. Loading one runs whatever the stream tells the "
"interpreter to run, which is why a checkpoint in that format is a risk of "
"its own — separate from its license, and separate from any CVE. For a model "
"on HuggingFace, BomLens reports what the Hub's own scan found. A file nobody "
"published has no such record, so the scan runs here instead, with "
"[picklescan](https://github.com/mmaitre314/picklescan) — the same tool the "
"Hub uses."
msgstr ""
"pickle 不是資料格式。載入的那一刻，資料流指示解譯器執行什麼就執行什麼，所以這"
"種格式的檢查點本身就是一項風險——與它的授權條款無關，也與任何 CVE 無關。對 "
"HuggingFace 上的模型，BomLens 會回報 Hub 自己的掃描結果。沒有人發佈過的檔案沒"
"有這種紀錄，因此改在本機掃描，用的是 [picklescan](https://github.com/"
"mmaitre314/picklescan)——與 Hub 相同的工具。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:107
msgid ""
"The verdict lands on the model component and feeds the file-security axis of "
"the risk assessment:"
msgstr "判定結果會落在模型元件上，並成為風險評估中檔案安全這一軸的依據："

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:115
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Verdict | Meaning | Assessment |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| Code-execution globals found | a dangerous global such as `os.system` is reachable | caution |\n"
"| Globals that need a look | something that could be code, typically a custom class | review |\n"
"| No code-execution globals | the pickle payload was parsed and held nothing of the kind | ok |\n"
"| Format does not execute code | GGUF, safetensors, ONNX, plain npy | ok |\n"
"| Could not be read | the file did not parse | review |\n"
msgstr ""
"| 判定 | 含意 | 評估 |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| 發現會執行程式碼的全域項目 | 可以觸及 `os.system` 這類危險的全域項目 | caution |\n"
"| 發現需檢視的全域項目 | 可能是程式碼的東西，通常是自訂類別 | review |\n"
"| 未發現會執行程式碼的全域項目 | pickle 內容已經剖析，其中沒有這類項目 | ok |\n"
"| 此格式不會執行程式碼 | GGUF、safetensors、ONNX、單純的 npy | ok |\n"
"| 無法讀取 | 檔案無法剖析 | review |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:117
msgid ""
"Two things worth knowing about the middle rows. \"Globals that need a look\" "
"is common in perfectly legitimate checkpoints — a model class of its own is "
"enough to trigger it — so it asks for a human rather than raising an alarm. "
"And a clean result answers one question only: it says the weights do not "
"execute code on load, not that the file has been cleared of everything. It "
"is a pickle analysis, not a malware scan."
msgstr ""
"中間兩列有兩件事值得知道。「發現需檢視的全域項目」在完全正當的檢查點中很常見"
"——模型帶有自己的類別就足以觸發——所以它是請人來看一眼，而不是拉警報。而乾淨的"
"結果只回答了一個問題：它說的是權重在載入時不會執行程式碼，不是說這個檔案什麼"
"問題都沒有。這是 pickle 分析，不是惡意程式掃描。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:119
msgid ""
"An `.npz` is opened and only the members that actually hold a pickle are "
"examined: a numpy array of dtype `object` stores its contents as a pickle, "
"which is how a payload hides in what looks like a numeric archive. A file "
"with no such member is reported as not applicable rather than as clean, "
"because nothing was examined."
msgstr ""
"`.npz` 會被打開，而且只檢查真正含有 pickle 的成員：dtype 為 `object` 的 "
"numpy 陣列會把內容存成 pickle，這正是酬載藏身在看似數值壓縮檔裡的路徑。沒有這"
"種成員的檔案會回報為不適用，而不是乾淨，因為並沒有檢查到任何東西。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:121
msgid ""
"If the scan cannot run at all, no verdict is written and the assessment "
"simply has no file-security axis. A missing scan reads as \"not scanned\", "
"never as safe."
msgstr ""
"如果掃描根本無法執行，就不會寫下任何判定，評估中也不會出現檔案安全這一軸。沒"
"掃描就讀成「未掃描」，絕不會讀成安全。"

#. type: Title ####
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "What this path cannot do"
msgstr "這條路徑做不到的事"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:125
msgid ""
"Two things, by construction. It has no model card, so the G7 checks that ask "
"about training data, intended use and evaluation report as gaps — "
"accurately, since the file says nothing about them. And it describes one "
"file: a model split into shards is currently scanned a shard at a time."
msgstr ""
"有兩件，出於設計。它沒有模型卡，所以 G7 中詢問訓練資料、預期用途與評估的檢查"
"會回報為缺漏——這是準確的，因為檔案對這些一字未提。另外它描述的是單一檔案：分"
"成多個分片 (shard) 的模型，目前是一個分片掃描一次。"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:126
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reading the result"
msgstr "讀懂結果"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:129
msgid "In the web UI, an AI/ML SBOM adds two sections to the left rail."
msgstr "在網頁介面中，AI/ML SBOM 會在左側導覽多出兩個區段。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:131
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Models & datasets** — each model card's identifier, architecture, task, license, supplier and integrity, a four-axis disclosure panel (weights / architecture / training data / training process, as documented in the BOM), and a table of the datasets the model references with each one's license, content digest and upstream.\n"
msgstr "**模型與資料集**——每張模型卡的識別碼、架構、任務、授權條款、供應者與完整性，一組四軸揭露面板（權重／架構／訓練資料／訓練過程，以 BOM 中記載的內容為準），以及一張列出模型所參考資料集的表格，附上每個資料集的授權條款、內容雜湊值與上游來源。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:133 docs/reference/ui.md:118
msgid ""
"![Models & datasets — model card and disclosure axes](../images/web-ui-"
"models.png)"
msgstr "![模型與資料集——模型卡與揭露四軸](../images/web-ui-models.png)"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:135
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Conformance** — for an AI-model SBOM this section adds the G7 minimum-element checks (all advisory), grouped by the seven G7 clusters, alongside the base format-conformance checks. Each element shows what it is and how to satisfy it. The next section explains what the numbers and badges mean.\n"
msgstr "**SBOM 符合性**——對 AI 模型 SBOM 來說，這個區段會在基本的格式符合性檢查之外，加上 G7 最低要素檢查（全部為建議性質），並依 G7 的七個叢集分組。每個要素都會說明它是什麼，以及如何滿足它。下一節解釋這些數字與標記的含意。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:137
msgid ""
"![Conformance — the G7 advisory sub-block for an AI SBOM](../images/web-ui-"
"g7.png)"
msgstr "![SBOM 符合性——AI SBOM 的 G7 建議子區塊](../images/web-ui-g7.png)"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:139
msgid ""
"The same data is in the artifacts: the ML-BOM (`_bom.json`, CycloneDX 1.7) "
"and the conformance report (`_conformance.*`)."
msgstr ""
"同樣的資料也在產出物裡：ML-BOM（`_bom.json`，CycloneDX 1.7）與符合性報告"
" (`_conformance.*`)。"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:140 docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reading the conformance report"
msgstr "如何讀符合性報告 {#reading-the-conformance-report}"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:143
msgid ""
"The G7 block leads with a headline such as \"N / 41 present\". The "
"denominator counts only the checks that have an automated source — 41 of the "
"51 — so the number states what the tool could verify on its own. The 10 "
"review-only elements appear next to it as a separate \"need review\" count, "
"and any automated check that found nothing is counted as advisory."
msgstr ""
"G7 區塊開頭是一行像「N / 41 已具備」的摘要數字。分母只計入有自動化來源的檢查"
"——51 項中的 41 項——所以這個數字說的是工具憑自己能驗證到什麼程度。那 10 項只能"
"人工檢視的要素會另外以「需人工檢視」的件數列在旁邊，而自動檢查中什麼都沒找到"
"的，則計為建議件數。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:145
msgid ""
"Each check has one of three statuses. Pass means the element is present in "
"the ML-BOM. Warn means it is missing or could not be confirmed; the 10 "
"review-only elements always show this status, labeled as requiring human "
"review. Fail does not occur for G7 checks in practice: every G7 element is "
"advisory, so a missing one never fails the SBOM as a whole. An overall fail "
"verdict can only come from the base format checks — the required CycloneDX "
"ones."
msgstr ""
"每項檢查都有三種狀態之一。通過 (pass) 表示該要素存在於 ML-BOM 中。建議"
" (warn) 表示它缺漏或無法確認；那 10 項只能人工檢視的要素一律是這個狀態，並標"
"示為需人工檢視。未通過 (fail) 在 G7 檢查中實際上不會出現：每一項 G7 要素都屬"
"建議性質，因此少了一項絕不會讓整份 SBOM 未通過。整體的未通過判定只可能來自基"
"本格式檢查，也就是 CycloneDX 的必要項目。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:147
msgid ""
"Some rows read \"not applicable\" instead, with a count of their own in the "
"summary. Those are checks the document gives nothing to judge: a coverage "
"percentage over zero components, or dependency relationships in a document "
"whose only subject is the model itself. They leave both sides of the "
"fraction rather than counting as met, because crediting them would put a "
"card that declares less above one that declares its datasets and is measured "
"on them. They are not review items either — a reviewer has nothing to look "
"at. A model card that names its training datasets therefore has more checks "
"actually measured, and a smaller denominator is not a better result."
msgstr ""
"有些列讀出來是不適用，並在摘要中另有自己的件數。這些是文件沒有給出任何判斷依"
"據的檢查：對零個元件計算涵蓋率，或是在只以模型本身為對象的文件裡詢問元件之間"
"的相依關係。它們會從分子與分母兩邊同時扣除，而不是算成已具備，因為算成已具備"
"會讓一張宣告較少的模型卡，排在有宣告資料集、因此被實際衡量的模型卡之上。它們"
"也不是需人工檢視的項目——檢視者根本沒有東西可看。因此，列出訓練資料集的模型卡"
"實際被衡量的檢查更多，分母較小並不代表結果更好。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:149
msgid "A source badge on each row says where a satisfied value comes from:"
msgstr "每一列上的來源標記會說明已滿足的值從哪裡來："

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:154
msgid "Auto (22 checks) — read directly from a field of the ML-BOM."
msgstr "自動（22 項）——直接從 ML-BOM 的欄位讀取。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:154
msgid ""
"Inferred (15) — derived from signals in the BOM rather than a single "
"dedicated field."
msgstr "推斷（15 項）——由 BOM 中的訊號導出，而非某個專用欄位。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:154
msgid ""
"Declared (4) — present only when a person or a manifest supplied the value."
msgstr "已宣告（4 項）——只有在人或資訊清單提供了這個值時才會出現。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:154
msgid ""
"Review needed (10) — no automated source exists; a person has to confirm it. "
"The same result ships in three formats: `{Project}_{Version}"
"_conformance.json` for machines (CI gates, diffing), `_conformance.md` as a "
"readable table, and `_conformance.html` as a visual summary. Each format "
"also carries the [regulatory crosswalk](#regulatory-crosswalk); in JSON it "
"is the `regulatoryCrosswalk` object, present only when at least one mapped "
"check was evaluated."
msgstr ""
"需人工檢視（10 項）——沒有自動化來源，必須由人確認。同一份結果會以三種格式輸"
"出：給機器讀的 `{Project}_{Version}_conformance.json`（CI 關卡、比對差異）、"
"表格形式的 `_conformance.md`，以及視覺化摘要的 `_conformance.html`。每一種格"
"式也都帶有[法規對照](#regulatory-crosswalk)；在 JSON 中它是 "
"`regulatoryCrosswalk` 物件，只有在至少評估過一項有對應的檢查時才會出現。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:156
msgid ""
"The report shows how to close a gap, not only that one exists. Every "
"advisory element with an automated source that is still absent carries a "
"CycloneDX fragment and a link to the authoritative documentation — in the "
"HTML, behind the \"Evidence / how to fill\" cell on that row; in the "
"Markdown, gathered under \"How to fill the gaps\". Passing and review-only "
"elements are left out, so a well-documented model shows none of this."
msgstr ""
"報告不只告訴你哪裡有缺漏，也告訴你怎麼補。每一項有自動化來源、卻仍然缺席的建"
"議要素，都會附上一段 CycloneDX 片段與權威文件的連結——在 HTML 中收在該列的「佐"
"證 · 方式」欄位裡，在 Markdown 中則彙整在「如何填補缺漏」底下。已通過與只能人"
"工檢視的要素不會列入，因此文件寫得完整的模型什麼都不會顯示。"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:157
#, no-wrap
msgid "A worked example"
msgstr "實際範例"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:160
msgid ""
"A concrete run helps read the rest. `FINAL-Bench/Aether-7B-5Attn` is a "
"foundation model published on HuggingFace under Apache-2.0 with its weights, "
"architecture, training data and training process all disclosed, so it shows "
"what a well-documented card produces."
msgstr ""
"親手跑一次會讓後面的內容好讀得多。`FINAL-Bench/Aether-7B-5Attn` 是發佈在 "
"HuggingFace 上、採用 Apache-2.0 的基礎模型，權重、架構、訓練資料與訓練過程全"
"部揭露，正好展示文件完整的模型卡會產出什麼。"

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:161
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --project Aether-7B-5Attn --version 1.0 \\\n"
"  --model \"FINAL-Bench/Aether-7B-5Attn\" --generate-only\n"
msgstr ""
"./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --project Aether-7B-5Attn --version 1.0 \\\n"
"  --model \"FINAL-Bench/Aether-7B-5Attn\" --generate-only\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:167
msgid ""
"The run reports `result=pass` with 33 of 41 G7 elements present. All 14 "
"Models-cluster checks pass, and the disclosure panel reads open on every "
"axis:"
msgstr ""
"這次執行回報 `result=pass`，41 項 G7 要素中已具備 33 項。模型叢集的 14 項檢查"
"全部通過，揭露面板的四個軸都讀為開放："

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:174
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Axis | Value |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| Weights | open-weight |\n"
"| Architecture | open-architecture |\n"
"| Training data | open-data |\n"
"| Training process | open-training |\n"
msgstr ""
"| 軸 | 值 |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| 權重 | open-weight |\n"
"| 架構 | open-architecture |\n"
"| 訓練資料 | open-data |\n"
"| 訓練過程 | open-training |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:176
msgid ""
"Because the card lists its datasets, BomLens looks up all seven the model "
"was trained on (FineWeb-Edu, the SmolLM corpus, FineMath, open-web-math, an "
"OpenCoder code corpus, and two Korean sets from HAERAE-HUB) and records what "
"each one declares. Eight of the ten Dataset-properties elements come back "
"present. The two that remain are the statistical properties of the data and "
"whether it contains personal or copyrighted material; neither can be read "
"from a repository, so the report asks a person rather than guessing."
msgstr ""
"由於模型卡列出了資料集，BomLens 逐一查詢了模型訓練所用的全部七個資料集"
"（FineWeb-Edu、SmolLM 語料庫、FineMath、open-web-math、一組 OpenCoder 程式碼"
"語料庫，以及 HAERAE-HUB 的兩組韓文資料集），並記錄下每一個所宣告的內容。資料"
"集屬性的十項要素中有八項回報為已具備。剩下的兩項是資料的統計屬性，以及它是否"
"含有個人資料或受著作權保護的內容；這兩項都無法從儲存庫讀出，因此報告不做猜"
"測，而是請人確認。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:178
msgid ""
"The lookup is what makes the next part visible. Three of the seven datasets "
"carry a license — `odc-by` on the FineWeb-Edu family, MIT on the OpenCoder "
"corpus — and three declare none at all: both HAERAE-HUB sets and open-web-"
"math. Counting dataset names would have called this model's training data "
"fully open. Reading the datasets shows a model published under Apache-2.0 "
"whose training corpus is, in part, of unstated license. That is not a "
"finding the tool judges; it is the one a reviewer needs before release, and "
"it only appears once each dataset is looked up."
msgstr ""
"正是這番查詢讓接下來這件事顯現出來。七個資料集中只有三個帶有授權條款——"
"FineWeb-Edu 家族是 `odc-by`，OpenCoder 語料庫是 MIT——另外三個完全沒有宣告："
"HAERAE-HUB 的兩組與 open-web-math。若只清點資料集名稱，這個模型的訓練資料會被"
"說成完全開放。實際讀過資料集後才看得出來：一個以 Apache-2.0 發佈的模型，它的"
"訓練語料有一部分授權條款不明。這不是工具該做的判斷；這是檢視者在發佈之前需要"
"知道的事，而它只有在逐一查詢每個資料集之後才會浮現。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:180
msgid ""
"The report this run produced is here to open as-is: the [conformance report]"
"(../samples/aether-7b-5attn_conformance.html) for the base model, which "
"opens with the same G7 rollup the AI compliance profile carries in JSON and "
"Markdown. Add `--lang ko` or `--lang zh-TW` for the same reports in Korean "
"or Traditional Chinese; the SBOM and the JSON reports stay English either "
"way."
msgstr ""
"這次執行產生的報告就在這裡，可以直接打開：基礎模型的[符合性報告](../samples/"
"aether-7b-5attn_conformance.html)，它的開頭就是 AI 合規概況在 JSON 與 "
"Markdown 中所帶的同一份 G7 彙整。加上 `--lang ko` 或 `--lang zh-TW` 可以得到"
"韓文或正體中文的同一批報告；無論哪一種，SBOM 與 JSON 報告都維持英文。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:184
msgid ""
"A report is not a finished review. Some elements a tool can fill; others "
"only a person can."
msgstr "報告不等於檢視完成。有些要素工具可以補上，有些只有人能回答。"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:188
msgid ""
"Fill the elements that have an automated source but came back empty, then "
"scan again. The shape that satisfies each one sits on its own row in the "
"report."
msgstr ""
"把有自動化來源但回報為空的要素填好，然後重新掃描。能滿足每一項的寫法就在報告"
"中它自己那一列。"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:188
msgid ""
"Answer the 10 review-only elements yourself — things like training-data "
"sensitivity or the intended application area, which no model card field can "
"prove."
msgstr ""
"自行回答那 10 項只能人工檢視的要素——像是訓練資料的敏感度或預期應用領域，這些"
"沒有任何模型卡欄位能證明。"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:188
msgid ""
"Check separately what this tool does not look at, such as training dataset "
"licensing and personal data."
msgstr "另外確認這個工具不看的事項，例如訓練資料集的授權條款與個人資料。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:190
msgid ""
"If you are preparing a model for release inside a company, the approval "
"steps and the pre-release checks live alongside this: see [Releasing an AI "
"model](https://sktelecom.github.io/guide/release/ai-model/) in the SK "
"Telecom open source guide."
msgstr ""
"如果你是在公司內部準備發佈 AI 模型，核准流程與發佈前的檢查項目就在旁邊：請看 "
"SK Telecom 開放原始碼指南中的[發佈 AI 模型](https://sktelecom.github.io/"
"guide/release/ai-model/)。"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:191
#, no-wrap
msgid "The G7 checklist"
msgstr "G7 檢查清單"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:194
msgid ""
"\"G7 Software Bill of Materials for AI — Minimum Elements\" is a guideline "
"published in May 2026 under the G7, led by Germany's BSI and Italy's ACN. It "
"defines 50 minimum elements, grouped into seven clusters, that an SBOM for "
"an AI model should carry: who made the model, what it is, what data it was "
"trained on, how it is secured, and how it performs. It is a non-binding "
"recommendation, not a regulation."
msgstr ""
"「G7 Software Bill of Materials for AI — Minimum Elements」是 2026 年 5 月以 "
"G7 名義發佈的指引，由德國 BSI 與義大利 ACN 主導。它定義了 50 項最低要素，分為"
"七個叢集，說明 AI 模型的 SBOM 應該承載什麼：誰做了這個模型、它是什麼、用什麼"
"資料訓練、如何受到保護，以及它的表現如何。這是不具約束力的建議，不是法規。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:196
msgid ""
"It still matters for regulation. The EU AI Act's high-risk and transparency "
"obligations apply from 2 August 2026, and the technical documentation its "
"Annex IV asks for overlaps substantially with the G7 clusters. BomLens does "
"not certify compliance with either text. What the conformance report gives "
"you is visibility: element by element, it shows what your model's "
"documentation already covers and what a person still has to supply — a "
"concrete way to prepare, not a compliance verdict."
msgstr ""
"它對法規仍然重要。EU AI Act 的高風險與透明性義務自 2026 年 8 月 2 日起適用，"
"而其 Annex IV 所要求的技術文件與 G7 叢集有相當程度的重疊。BomLens 不認證是否"
"符合這兩份文本中的任何一份。符合性報告給你的是可見性：它逐項顯示你的模型文件"
"已經涵蓋了什麼、還有什麼必須由人提供——這是一條具體的準備途徑，不是合規判定。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:198
msgid ""
"BomLens shows the 50 elements as 51 checks. Model openness (whether weights, "
"architecture, training data and training process are disclosed) is one facet "
"of the Model license element in the G7 text, but it is worth seeing on its "
"own, so it gets a separate row."
msgstr ""
"BomLens 把這 50 項要素呈現為 51 項檢查。模型開放性（權重、架構、訓練資料與訓"
"練過程是否揭露）在 G7 原文中是 Model license 要素的一個面向，但它值得單獨看，"
"所以另立一列。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:208
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Cluster | Checks | Of which need human review |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| Metadata | 10 | 0 |\n"
"| System-level properties | 9 | 4 |\n"
"| Models | 14 | 0 |\n"
"| Dataset properties | 10 | 2 |\n"
"| Infrastructure | 2 | 0 |\n"
"| Security properties | 4 | 3 |\n"
"| Key performance indicators | 2 | 1 |\n"
msgstr ""
"| 叢集 | 檢查數 | 其中需人工檢視 |\n"
"| --- | --- | --- |\n"
"| 後設資料 | 10 | 0 |\n"
"| 系統層級屬性 | 9 | 4 |\n"
"| 模型 | 14 | 0 |\n"
"| 資料集屬性 | 10 | 2 |\n"
"| 基礎設施 | 2 | 0 |\n"
"| 安全性屬性 | 4 | 3 |\n"
"| 關鍵績效指標 | 2 | 1 |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:210
msgid ""
"Ten elements have no automated source — things like the intended application "
"area or dataset sensitivity, which no model-card field can prove. BomLens "
"lists them as requiring human review instead of guessing."
msgstr ""
"有 10 項要素沒有自動化來源——像是預期應用領域或資料集敏感度，這些沒有任何模型"
"卡欄位能證明。BomLens 不做猜測，而是把它們列為需人工檢視。"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:211
#, no-wrap
msgid "Regulatory crosswalk"
msgstr "法規對照 {#regulatory-crosswalk}"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:214
msgid ""
"The conformance report links each check that maps to a regulation to the "
"specific documentation obligation it touches. It answers a reviewer's "
"question: when a check comes back short, which regulatory requirement does "
"that gap concern? The reference sits under the requirement it belongs to in "
"the check tables, and a crosswalk section above the detail rolls the "
"coverage up — one row per framework, counting how many mapped checks are "
"present, a gap, or review-only."
msgstr ""
"符合性報告會把每一項有對應法規的檢查，連到它所觸及的具體文件化義務。它回答的"
"是檢視者的問題：某項檢查結果不足時，這個缺漏牽涉到哪一條法規要求？參考出處放"
"在檢查表格中它所屬要求的下方，而明細之上的法規對照區段則把涵蓋範圍彙總起來——"
"每個框架一列，統計已對應的檢查中有多少項已具備、多少項缺漏、多少項只能人工檢"
"視。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:216
msgid "Two frameworks cover every analyzed SBOM, AI or not:"
msgstr "有兩個框架涵蓋所有被分析的 SBOM，無論是不是 AI："

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:219
msgid ""
"EU Cyber Resilience Act — via BSI TR-03183-2, the German technical guideline "
"written for CRA compliance and the most detailed public SBOM field "
"specification (the CRA itself names no data fields). TR-03183-2 is a "
"national guideline, and the European harmonized standard that will carry the "
"binding wording is still a draft."
msgstr ""
"EU Cyber Resilience Act (EU CRA)——透過 BSI TR-03183-2 連結，那是德國為 CRA "
"合規所撰寫的技術指引，也是目前公開文件中最詳盡的 SBOM 欄位規格（CRA 本文並未"
"指名任何資料欄位）。TR-03183-2 是國家層級的指引，而將承載具約束力條文的歐洲調"
"和標準目前仍是草案。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:219
msgid ""
"US SBOM minimum elements — the 17 data fields and 6 practices of the 2026 "
"minimum elements, published by CISA, the NSA and the FBI with fifteen "
"international partners and replacing the NTIA elements of 2021. Federal SBOM "
"collection has since been narrowed to agency-level, risk-based decisions, "
"but the fields remain the practical baseline that individual agencies ask "
"for."
msgstr ""
"美國 SBOM 最低要素——2026 年版最低要素的 17 個資料欄位與 6 項實務作法，由 "
"CISA、NSA 與 FBI 會同十五個國際夥伴發佈，取代 2021 年的 NTIA 要素。聯邦層級"
"的 SBOM 蒐集後來已收斂為各機關依風險自行決定，但這些欄位仍是個別機關實際會要"
"求的實務基準。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:221
msgid "For an AI SBOM, two more frameworks map onto the G7 elements:"
msgstr "對 AI SBOM 來說，另有兩個框架對應到 G7 要素："

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:224
msgid ""
"EU AI Act — the technical-documentation sections of Annex IV (Regulation "
"(EU) 2024/1689, Article 11(1))."
msgstr ""
"EU AI Act——Annex IV 的技術文件章節 (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689, Article "
"11(1))。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:224
msgid ""
"AI Framework Act (Korea) — the Act's articles on transparency (제31조), "
"safety and risk management (제32조), high-impact AI (제33·34조), and impact "
"assessment (제35조). The Act sets framework-level duties, so these links are "
"coarser than the EU ones."
msgstr ""
"AI 基本法（韓國）——該法關於透明性 (제31조)、安全性與風險管理 (제32조)、高影"
"響 AI (제33·34조) 與影響評估 (제35조) 的條文。這部法律訂的是框架層級的義務，"
"因此這些連結比 EU 的更為粗略。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:226
msgid ""
"The crosswalk is a preparation aid, not a compliance verdict. BomLens does "
"not certify compliance with any of these texts, and the report says so in "
"the section itself. Each mapping carries the interpretive basis for the link "
"so a person can judge it, and the crosswalk never changes a check's status "
"or the overall result — it only regroups findings the checks already "
"produced."
msgstr ""
"法規對照是準備用的輔助，不是合規判定。BomLens 不認證是否符合上述任何一份文"
"本，報告也在該區段中明言這一點。每一組對應都附有建立該連結的解釋依據，讓人可"
"以自行判斷；法規對照也絕不會改變任何檢查的狀態或整體結果——它只是把檢查已經產"
"生的結果重新分組。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:228
msgid ""
"The mapping lives in `docker/lib/regulation-crosswalk.json`, keyed by check "
"id — the G7 element ids for the AI checks and the plain CycloneDX check ids "
"for the base format checks. It is deliberately conservative: only checks "
"with a defensible correspondence are mapped (38 today), and a test validates "
"every mapped id against the registry so the crosswalk cannot drift silently "
"when a check is renamed."
msgstr ""
"對應關係放在 `docker/lib/regulation-crosswalk.json`，以檢查 id 為鍵——AI 檢查"
"用 G7 要素 id，基本格式檢查用一般的 CycloneDX 檢查 id。它刻意保守：只有具備可"
"辯護對應關係的檢查才會納入（目前 38 項），並且有測試會拿每一個已對應的 id 去"
"核對登錄表，讓檢查更名時法規對照不會默默失準。"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:229
#, no-wrap
msgid "AI compliance profile"
msgstr "AI 合規概況"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:232
msgid ""
"For an AI SBOM, BomLens also writes a one-page AI compliance profile (`_ai-"
"profile.{json,md,html}`) that gathers into one place what otherwise lives "
"across separate artifacts: the G7 status by cluster, the regulatory "
"crosswalk, and the components whose license is flagged for review (AI "
"behavioral-use or non-commercial). It runs no scan and makes no compliance "
"determination — it regroups findings the pipeline already produced, so a "
"reviewer can read the whole picture at a glance. It is written for the AI-"
"model (`--model`) and supplier-SBOM (`--analyze`) paths, and is a no-op for "
"a plain (non-AI) SBOM."
msgstr ""
"對 AI SBOM，BomLens 還會產出一份單頁的 AI 合規概況 (`_ai-profile."
"{json,md,html}`)，把原本散落在各個產出物中的內容彙整到一處：各叢集的 G7 狀"
"態、法規對照，以及授權條款被標記待檢視的元件（AI 行為限制或非商業）。它不執行"
"任何掃描，也不做任何合規判定——它只是把流程已經產生的結果重新分組，讓檢視者能"
"一眼讀完整體樣貌。它會在 AI 模型 (`--model`) 與供應者 SBOM (`--analyze`) 兩條"
"路徑上產生，對一般（非 AI）SBOM 則不做任何事。"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:233
#, no-wrap
msgid "Model risk assessment"
msgstr "模型風險評估"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:236
msgid ""
"The AI compliance profile also carries a usability verdict per model, "
"answering the question a development team asks first: can we use this model, "
"and under what conditions? Each model — and each dataset entry — is assessed "
"on the axes the pipeline has evidence for and given one of four verdicts."
msgstr ""
"AI 合規概況還為每個模型帶上一項可用性判定，回答開發團隊最先問的問題：我們可以"
"用這個模型嗎，在什麼條件下？每個模型——以及每個資料集項目——都會就流程有佐證的"
"那些軸進行評估，並得到四種判定之一。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:243
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Verdict | Meaning |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| ok | Only known unrestricted signals — for example a permissive license. |\n"
"| conditional | Usable when the listed conditions are met — for example the Llama community license's user threshold and naming rule, or a copyleft license's notice duties. |\n"
"| caution | A known blocking signal — for example a non-commercial or research-only license. |\n"
"| review | The tool cannot judge: an unrecognized license, a missing license, or a dataset that could not be read. A person has to look. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| 判定 | 含意 |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| 未發現限制訊號 (ok) | 只有已知的無限制訊號——例如寬鬆式的授權條款。 |\n"
"| 有條件使用 (conditional) | 滿足所列條件即可使用——例如 Llama 社群授權條款的使用者數門檻與命名規則，或是 copyleft 授權條款的聲明義務。 |\n"
"| 注意 (caution) | 存在已知的阻斷訊號——例如非商業或僅限研究的授權條款。 |\n"
"| 需人工檢視 (review) | 工具無法判定：無法辨識的授權條款、缺少授權條款，或是讀不到的資料集。必須由人來看。 |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:245
msgid ""
"The file-security axis reads the scan results Hugging Face itself runs over "
"every repository — ClamAV for malware and picklescan for executable pickle "
"imports, per file. BomLens reads them through the metadata API without "
"downloading a single file, records the worst status with the flagged file "
"names, and notes whether the weights use a pickle-family format (which can "
"execute code on load) or a safe one such as safetensors. A model whose scan "
"is still pending reads review, not safe. Set `ENRICH_HF_SECURITY=false` to "
"skip the lookup."
msgstr ""
"檔案安全這一軸讀的是 Hugging Face 自己對每個儲存庫執行的掃描結果——逐檔以 "
"ClamAV 找惡意程式，以 picklescan 找可執行的 pickle import。BomLens 透過後設資"
"料 API 讀取這些結果，一個檔案都不下載，記錄下最差的狀態與被標記的檔名，並註明"
"權重使用的是 pickle 家族的格式（載入時可能執行程式碼）還是像 safetensors 這樣"
"安全的格式。掃描還在等待中的模型讀成需人工檢視，不是安全。設定 "
"`ENRICH_HF_SECURITY=false` 可以略過這項查詢。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:247
msgid ""
"The license verdict comes from a curated registry (`docker/lib/ai-risk-"
"knowledge.json`) covering the complete Hugging Face license tag list. Each "
"entry records whether commercial use, redistribution and derivatives are "
"allowed, the conditions that apply, and a link to the license text; the "
"profile prints the summary and the conditions next to the verdict, so the "
"grounds travel with the judgement. A license the registry does not know "
"falls to review — it is never guessed. A model's overall verdict is the "
"worst across its assessed axes, and an axis nothing evaluated shows as not "
"assessed rather than being read as safe."
msgstr ""
"授權條款判定來自一份人工整理的知識庫 (`docker/lib/ai-risk-knowledge.json`)，"
"涵蓋 Hugging Face 完整的授權條款標籤清單。每一筆都記錄了是否允許商業使用、再"
"散布與製作衍生物，適用哪些條件，以及授權條款原文的連結；概況會把摘要與條件印"
"在判定旁邊，讓依據隨著判定一起移動。知識庫不認識的授權條款會落到需人工檢視——"
"絕不猜測。模型的綜合判定取它所評估各軸中最差的一項，而什麼都沒評估到的軸會顯"
"示為未評估，不會被讀成安全。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:249
msgid ""
"Two further checks deepen the license verdict. For a model tagged `other`, "
"BomLens reads the repository's LICENSE file (one small text file — still no "
"weight download) and searches it for restrictive wording such as non-"
"commercial, research-only or no-derivatives clauses; a match is quoted "
"verbatim next to the verdict, so the report says \"review needed because of "
"this sentence\" rather than only \"unclassified\". No match still reads "
"review — a pattern miss proves nothing. And for a fine-tuned model, BomLens "
"walks the declared base-model chain (up to five ancestors) and compares "
"licenses: when an ancestor carries a license whose conditions extend to "
"derivatives (Llama, Gemma, the RAIL family, non-commercial CC) but the model "
"itself declares something else, the mismatch is flagged as a caution — a "
"common mislabeling on the hub that a tag-only check cannot see."
msgstr ""
"還有兩項檢查讓授權條款判定更深入。對標籤為 `other` 的模型，BomLens 會讀取儲存"
"庫的 LICENSE 檔案（一個小小的文字檔——仍然不下載權重），並在其中搜尋非商業、僅"
"限研究或禁止製作衍生物之類的限制性字句；命中的字句會逐字引用在判定旁邊，讓報"
"告說的是「因為這句話所以需要檢視」，而不只是「未分類」。沒有命中仍然讀成需人"
"工檢視——樣式沒中什麼也證明不了。而對微調過的模型，BomLens 會沿著所宣告的上游"
"模型鏈（base model，最多五代）比對授權條款：當某個上游帶有條件會延伸到衍生物"
"的授權條款（Llama、Gemma、RAIL 家族、非商業的 CC），而模型自己卻宣告了別的條"
"款時，這個不一致會被標為注意——這是 hub 上常見的標示錯誤，只看標籤的檢查看不出"
"來。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:251
msgid ""
"The datasets axis rolls the referenced datasets up into the model's verdict. "
"Each dataset entry is judged on its own license and on its declared risk "
"markers: a publisher tag such as `pii` (personally identifiable information) "
"or `not-for-all-audiences`, and an access restriction (gated or private "
"repository). The model takes the worst dataset verdict, with the offending "
"datasets named. These markers are the publisher's own declarations — their "
"absence proves nothing, so they only ever raise a verdict, never clear one."
msgstr ""
"資料集這一軸把所參考的資料集彙整進模型的判定。每個資料集項目會就它自己的授權"
"條款，以及它所宣告的風險標記來判定：發佈者標籤如 `pii`（個人可識別資訊）或 "
"`not-for-all-audiences`，以及存取限制（受管制或私有的儲存庫）。模型會取最差的"
"資料集判定，並指名是哪些資料集造成的。這些標記是發佈者自己的宣告——沒有標記什"
"麼也證明不了，所以它們只會拉高判定，絕不會解除判定。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:253
msgid ""
"The verdict can be tailored to how you will actually use the model. Pass `--"
"usage` with one of `internal` (in-house review and research), `product` "
"(shipping in a product or service), `redistribute` (fine-tuning and "
"redistribution) or `outputs-only` (using only what the model generates), and "
"only the license conditions that bind that scenario decide the verdict — a "
"non-commercial model, for example, reads conditional for internal research "
"but caution for product use. The report always states which scenario it "
"judged for; without `--usage` every condition counts."
msgstr ""
"判定可以依你實際打算怎麼用這個模型來調整。傳入 `--usage` 並指定 `internal`"
"（內部檢視與研究）、`product`（整合進產品或服務）、`redistribute`（微調並再散"
"布）或 `outputs-only`（只使用模型產生的輸出）之一，就只有約束該情境的授權條件"
"會決定判定——例如一個非商業的模型，用於內部研究會讀成有條件使用，用於產品整合"
"則是注意。報告一律會註明它是以哪個情境判定的；沒有 `--usage` 時，所有條件都計"
"入。"

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:254
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --project my-llm --version 1.0 \\\n"
"  --model \"meta-llama/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct\" --usage product --generate-only\n"
msgstr ""
"./scripts/scan-sbom.sh --project my-llm --version 1.0 \\\n"
"  --model \"meta-llama/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct\" --usage product --generate-only\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:260
msgid ""
"The verdicts are guidance, not legal advice, and every report that prints "
"them says so. They gather what a reviewer needs — the terms, the sources, "
"the unknowns — so the final decision is made by a person with the evidence "
"in one place."
msgstr ""
"這些判定是指引，不是法律意見，每一份印出它們的報告都會這麼說。它們把檢視者需"
"要的東西——條款、來源、未知之處——集中在一起，讓最終決定由掌握全部依據的人來"
"做。"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:261 docs/guides/firmware.md:96
#: docs/guides/supplier-sbom.md:165
#, no-wrap
msgid "Limits"
msgstr "限制"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:270
msgid ""
"A model the tool cannot read produces no SBOM at all. The generator fills "
"the card with generic defaults when a fetch fails, so BomLens checks its log "
"and refuses the run rather than handing back an inventory of placeholders "
"that would read as a pass."
msgstr ""
"工具讀不到的模型根本不會產生 SBOM。取得失敗時產生器會用通用的預設值把模型卡填"
"滿，因此 BomLens 會檢查它的日誌並拒絕這次執行，而不是回傳一份滿是佔位值、看起"
"來卻像通過的清單。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:270
msgid ""
"The result is only as complete as the HuggingFace model card. A sparse card "
"yields a sparse ML-BOM, and the G7 checks reflect what the card documents — "
"not an audit of the model."
msgstr ""
"結果的完整程度只會等於 HuggingFace 模型卡本身。內容單薄的模型卡產出單薄的 ML-"
"BOM，而 G7 檢查反映的是模型卡記載了什麼——不是對模型本身的稽核。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:270
msgid ""
"Dataset entries record what a dataset declares about itself. Whether the "
"declared license is the right one, and whether a derived dataset is "
"compatible with the ones it came from, is a judgement the report leaves to a "
"reviewer."
msgstr ""
"資料集項目記錄的是該資料集對自己的宣告。所宣告的授權條款是否正確，以及衍生出"
"來的資料集是否與它的來源相容，報告都留給檢視者判斷。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:270
msgid ""
"A compound SPDX license expression (`MIT OR Apache-2.0`) is assessed as a "
"whole rather than by resolving the choice, so a dual-licensed model can read "
"`review` where either option alone would be `ok`. The direction is "
"deliberately cautious — it never under-warns — but it may over-flag; the "
"report names the exact expression so a reviewer can confirm."
msgstr ""
"複合的 SPDX 授權條款表達式 (`MIT OR Apache-2.0`) 會整體評估，不會去解析其中的"
"選擇，因此一個雙重授權的模型可能讀成 `review`，即使單獨採用任一邊都會是 "
"`ok`。這個方向刻意保守——它絕不會低估警示——但可能過度標記；報告會寫出確切的表"
"達式，讓檢視者自行確認。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:270
msgid ""
"The conformance report does not certify compliance with the EU AI Act or any "
"other regulation. It makes documentation gaps visible so a person can close "
"them."
msgstr ""
"符合性報告不認證是否符合 EU AI Act 或任何其他法規。它讓文件缺漏顯而易見，好讓"
"人去補。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:270
msgid ""
"It fetches metadata over the network, so offline use is not supported. "
"Private and gated models need `HF_TOKEN` (see [Private and gated models]"
"(#private-and-gated-models))."
msgstr ""
"它會透過網路取得後設資料，因此不支援離線使用。私有與受管制的模型需要 "
"`HF_TOKEN`（參考[私有與受管制的模型](#private-and-gated-models)）。"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:270
msgid ""
"The model id must be `org/model`. A collection name or a full URL will not "
"resolve. ---"
msgstr "模型 id 必須是 `org/model`。集合名稱或完整 URL 無法解析。 ---"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/ai-model.md:271
#, no-wrap
msgid "> **Related**: [Pipeline by input type](../concepts/pipeline-by-input.md) | [Web UI reference](../reference/ui.md) | [CLI reference](../reference/cli.md)\n"
msgstr "> **相關文件**：[各輸入類型的流程](../concepts/pipeline-by-input.md) | [網頁介面參考](../reference/ui.md) | [CLI 參考](../reference/cli.md)\n"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#: docs/guides/by-input.md:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "How BomLens produces an SBOM, an open-source notice, and a risk report for seven input forms — a GitHub URL, a ZIP archive, local source, an existing SBOM, a Yocto build directory, firmware, and a HuggingFace AI model."
msgstr "BomLens 如何為七種輸入形式產生 SBOM、開放原始碼授權聲明與風險報告——GitHub URL、ZIP 壓縮檔、本機原始碼、既有的 SBOM、Yocto 建置目錄、韌體，以及 HuggingFace AI 模型。"

#. type: Title #
#: docs/guides/by-input.md:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Input scenarios guide"
msgstr "輸入情境指南"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/by-input.md:7 docs/guides/server-delivery.md:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "概觀"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/by-input.md:10
msgid ""
"An open-source compliance manager receives deliverables from many teams in "
"different forms. This guide shows how to produce the same three deliverables "
"for each of seven input forms. (An AI model differs slightly — an ML-BOM and "
"no security report; see Scenario 7.)"
msgstr ""
"開放原始碼合規負責人會從各個團隊收到形式各異的交付物。這份指南說明如何為七種"
"輸入形式產生同樣的三份產出物。（AI 模型稍有不同——產出的是 ML-BOM，而且沒有安"
"全報告；參考情境 7。）"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/by-input.md:12
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The three deliverables**\n"
msgstr "**三份產出物**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/by-input.md:18
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Deliverable | File | Meaning |\n"
"|-------------|------|---------|\n"
"| Open-source notice | `{Project}_{Version}_NOTICE.{txt,html}` | the notice that satisfies license obligations |\n"
"| SBOM | `{Project}_{Version}_bom.json` | CycloneDX 1.6 component inventory |\n"
"| Open-source risk report | `{Project}_{Version}_risk-report.{md,html}` | aggregated license + vulnerability risk (with deadlines) |\n"
msgstr ""
"| 產出物 | 檔案 | 說明 |\n"
"|-------------|------|---------|\n"
"| 開放原始碼授權聲明 | `{Project}_{Version}_NOTICE.{txt,html}` | 滿足授權條款義務的聲明文件 |\n"
"| SBOM | `{Project}_{Version}_bom.json` | CycloneDX 1.6 元件清冊 |\n"
"| 開放原始碼風險報告 | `{Project}_{Version}_risk-report.{md,html}` | 彙整授權條款與弱點的風險（含修補期限） |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/by-input.md:20
msgid ""
"For any input form, adding `--all --generate-only` produces all three at "
"once (the risk report is on by default and is only turned off with `--no-"
"report`)."
msgstr "無論哪一種輸入形式，加上 `--all --generate-only` 就會一次產生這三份（風險報告預設開啟，只有 `--no-report` 會把它關掉）。"

#. type: Title ##
#: docs/guides/by-input.md:21 docs/guides/server-delivery.md:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "Common setup"
msgstr "共通準備 {#common-setup}"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/by-input.md:28
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> **Windows**: the commands here are for macOS/Linux. Pick one of the following. See [Getting started](../start/first-scan.md) for installation.\n"
">\n"
"> - Replace `./scripts/scan-sbom.sh` with `scripts\\scan-sbom.bat` (needs Git Bash).\n"
"> - Under WSL2, run the commands as-is.\n"
"> - To work without a command line, double-click `scripts\\sbom-ui.bat`.\n"
msgstr ""
"> **Windows**：這裡的指令是以 macOS/Linux 為準。請從下列方式中選一種。安裝方式請看[快速開始](../start/first-scan.md)。\n"
">\n"
"> - 把 `./scripts/scan-sbom.sh` 換成 `scripts\\scan-sbom.bat`（需要 Git Bash）。\n"
"> - 在 WSL2 底下直接照原樣執行這些指令。\n"
"> - 不想用指令列的話，可以雙擊 `scripts\\sbom-ui.bat`。\n"

#. type: Fenced code block (bash)
#: docs/guides/by-input.md:29
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"# Docker 20.10+ required. Pull the scanner image once (or build it yourself).\n"
"docker pull ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens:latest   # legacy name sbom-scanner serves the same image\n"
"\n"
"# For convenience, keep the script path in a variable.\n"
"SBOM=/path/to/bomlens/scripts/scan-sbom.sh\n"
msgstr ""
"# 需要 Docker 20.10+。掃描器映像檔只需下載一次（也可以自己建置）。\n"
"docker pull ghcr.io/sktelecom/bomlens:latest   # 舊名稱 sbom-scanner 指向同一個映像檔\n"
"\n"
"# 為了方便，把指令碼路徑放進變數裡。\n"
"SBOM=/path/to/bomlens/scripts/scan-sbom.sh\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/by-input.md:40
msgid ""
"`$SBOM` in every command below is the script path variable from [Common "
"setup](#common-setup) — if you skipped that step, put the full path to `scan-"
"sbom.sh` in its place."
msgstr ""
"下面每一道指令裡的 `$SBOM`，都是[共通準備](#common-setup)中定義的指令碼路徑變"
"數——如果跳過了那一步，就把 `scan-sbom.sh` 的完整路徑直接填在它的位置。"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/by-input.md:54
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Input form | Mode | Core command (summary) | Deliverables |\n"
"|------------|------|------------------------|--------------|\n"
"| GitHub URL | SOURCE | `$SBOM --git <url> --all --generate-only` | notice, SBOM, risk report |\n"
"| Source ZIP | SOURCE | `$SBOM --target app.zip --all --generate-only` | same |\n"
"| Local directory (C/C++) | SOURCE | `cd dir && $SBOM --all --generate-only` | same |\n"
"| Existing SBOM JSON | ANALYZE | `$SBOM --analyze sbom.json --generate-only` | same + conformance report |\n"
"| Yocto build directory | ANALYZE | `$SBOM --target ~/poky/build --generate-only` | same + conformance report |\n"
"| Build artifact (`.jar`, `.deb`, …) | BINARY | `$SBOM --target app.jar --all --generate-only` | same |\n"
"| Installer (`.exe`, `.msi`, `.dmg`) | FIRMWARE | `$SBOM --target installer.exe --all --generate-only` | same |\n"
"| Mobile app (`.apk`, `.ipa`) | FIRMWARE | `$SBOM --target app.apk --all --generate-only` | same |\n"
"| Firmware `.bin` | FIRMWARE | `$SBOM --target dev.bin --firmware --all --generate-only` | same |\n"
"| AI model (HuggingFace) | AIBOM | `$SBOM --model owner/name --generate-only` | notice, ML-BOM (1.7), risk report (no security) |\n"
"| AI model file (GGUF, safetensors, …) | MODELFILE | `$SBOM --model-file ./model.gguf --generate-only` | notice, ML-BOM (1.7), risk report (no security) |\n"
msgstr ""
"| 輸入形式 | 模式 | 核心指令（摘要） | 產出物 |\n"
"|------------|------|------------------------|--------------|\n"
"| GitHub URL | SOURCE | `$SBOM --git <url> --all --generate-only` | 授權聲明、SBOM、風險報告 |\n"
"| 原始碼 ZIP | SOURCE | `$SBOM --target app.zip --all --generate-only` | 同上 |\n"
"| 本機目錄 (C/C++) | SOURCE | `cd dir && $SBOM --all --generate-only` | 同上 |\n"
"| 既有的 SBOM JSON | ANALYZE | `$SBOM --analyze sbom.json --generate-only` | 同上，另加符合性報告 |\n"
"| Yocto 建置目錄 | ANALYZE | `$SBOM --target ~/poky/build --generate-only` | 同上，另加符合性報告 |\n"
"| 建置產出物（`.jar`、`.deb`…） | BINARY | `$SBOM --target app.jar --all --generate-only` | 同上 |\n"
"| 安裝程式（`.exe`、`.msi`、`.dmg`） | FIRMWARE | `$SBOM --target installer.exe --all --generate-only` | 同上 |\n"
"| 行動應用程式（`.apk`、`.ipa`） | FIRMWARE | `$SBOM --target app.apk --all --generate-only` | 同上 |\n"
"| 韌體 `.bin` | FIRMWARE | `$SBOM --target dev.bin --firmware --all --generate-only` | 同上 |\n"
"| AI 模型 (HuggingFace) | AIBOM | `$SBOM --model owner/name --generate-only` | 授權聲明、ML-BOM (1.7)、風險報告（無安全報告） |\n"
"| AI 模型檔案（GGUF、safetensors…） | MODELFILE | `$SBOM --model-file ./model.gguf --generate-only` | 授權聲明、ML-BOM (1.7)、風險報告（無安全報告） |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/guides/by-input.md:58
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"> Every command also needs `--project <name> --version <version>` (see examples below).\n"
">\n"
"> C/C++ without a package manager (Conan/vcpkg): add `--identify-vendored` so open source copied straight into the sources is detected as named components. Strongly recommended for this case — see [Scenario 3](#scenario-3--local-cc-source-directory).\n"
msgstr ""
"> 每一道指令都還需要 `--project <name> --version <version>`（見下方範例）。\n"
">\n"
"> 沒有套件管理器（Conan／vcpkg）的 C/C++：請加上 `--identify-vendored`，直接複製進原始碼裡的開放原始碼才會被偵測為具名元件。這種情況強烈建議開啟——參考[情境 3](#scenario-3--local-cc-source-directory)。\n"

